{
  "email": "dana.whitfield@brightline.example",
  "reason": "Check account, mailbox usage, and devices per KB-009"
}

{
  "outcome": "resolved",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Dana, thanks for letting us know. Your mailbox is healthy: it's only about 17% full and still receiving mail, which is why your phone gets everything. Your laptop is also online with no warnings. That means the problem is with Outlook on the laptop itself. Please try these steps in order and check for new mail after each one:\n1. Open Outlook on the web in your browser to confirm your new mail is there.\n2. In Outlook on the laptop, go to the Send / Receive tab. If Work Offline is highlighted, click it to turn it off.\n3. Close Outlook completely and open it again.\n4. Restart your laptop.\n5. If it's still stuck, you can set up a fresh Outlook profile. Go to Control Panel > Mail > Show Profiles > Add, create a new profile, set it as the default, then open Outlook. Your mail will download again, which may take a little while. We're also happy to do this step for you.\nIf new mail doesn't show in Outlook on the web, or none of these steps work, just reply here and we'll take it further right away.",
  "internal_note": "User is the CEO (VIP). Reported that desktop Outlook stopped syncing this morning while mobile mail still works. Checked: mailbox at 17.4% (8,900 of 51,200 MB), so not over quota and KB-010 doesn't apply. Account is active with no lockout. Laptop BL-LT-0101 is online, last check-in 2026-10-09 14:21 UTC, 60% disk free, no warnings. Because the phone gets mail, the mailbox and service are fine, so this is a client-side Outlook problem (KB-009). Sent the user the KB-009 fix steps: check Work Offline, restart Outlook, restart the laptop, rebuild the profile. Since this is a VIP, consider offering hands-on or remote help with the profile rebuild if the first steps don't fix it. Escalate if Outlook on the web is also missing new mail, or if other users report the same problem.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-009",
    "KB-010"
  ],
  "confidence": "high"
}
